oid and horseshoe kidney: a frequent association of two rare entities--a case report and review of the literature</article-title><source>J Surg Oncol</source><year>1998</year><volume>68</volume><fpage>113</fpage><lpage>119</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9624041</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/(SICI)1096-9098(199806)68:2&#x0003c;113::AID-JSO8&#x0003e;3.0.CO;2-9</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>el-Naggar</surname><given-names>AK</given-names></name><name><surname>Troncoso</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Ordonez</surname><given-names>NG</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Primary renal carcinoid tumor with molecular abnormality characteristic of conventional renal cell neoplasms</article-title><source>Diagn Mol Pathol</source><year>1995</year><volume>4</volume><fpage>48</fpage><lpage>53</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7735556</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cauley</surname><given-names>JE</given-names></name><name><surname>Almagro</surname><given-names>UA</given-names></name><name><surname>Jacobs</surname><given-names>SC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Primary renal carcinoid tumor</article-title><source>Urology</source><year>1988</year><volume>32</volume><fpage>564</fpage><lpage>566</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3201667</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0090-4295(98)90046-2</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Krishnan</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Truong</surname><given-names>LD</given-names></name><name><surname>Saleh</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Sirbasku</surname><given-names>DM</given-names></name><name><surname>Slawin</surname><given-names>